{
  "id": "COMPOUND:43464 - PROTEIN:5011",
  "verbalization": "Alloocimene, (4Z,6Z)- is implicated in the biological pathway leading to HCC1937 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Alloocimene acts as a target for Carboxylesterase 2, which in turn is targeted by 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. This compound is also a target of HCC1937, indicating a complex network of interactions where Alloocimene indirectly influences HCC1937 via the enzyme and its substrate. The pathway highlights a potential role for Alloocimene in modulating the activity of 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, which ultimately affects HCC1937. The evidence supports a mechanism where Alloocimene serves as a mediator in the interaction with the enzyme and its downstream target, suggesting a possible role in the regulation of HCC1937 through enzymatic pathways.",
